foundation.question_text:
One layer has $3$ rows of $4$ cubes. There are $2$ layers. Find the total.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,3);
\draw (1,0)--(1,3);
\draw (2,0)--(2,3);
\draw (3,0)--(3,3);
\draw (4,0)--(4,3);
\draw (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw (0,1)--(4,1);
\draw (0,2)--(4,2);
\draw (0,3)--(4,3);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2\text{ identical layers}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

One layer has $2$ rows of $5$ cubes. There are $4$ layers. Find the volume.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2);
\draw (1,0)--(1,2);
\draw (2,0)--(2,2);
\draw (3,0)--(3,2);
\draw (4,0)--(4,2);
\draw (5,0)--(5,2);
\draw (0,0)--(5,0);
\draw (0,1)--(5,1);
\draw (0,2)--(5,2);
\node[below] at (2.5,0) {$4\text{ identical layers}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

